articles.content_en:
The Standing Committee of the National People's Congress has discussed the meaning of the "organization with the characteristics of a mafia-style gang" as stipulated in paragraph 1 of Article 294 of the Criminal Law, and gives the following interpretation:
The "organization with the characteristics of a mafia-style gang" as stipulated in paragraph 1 of Article 294 of the Criminal Law shall concurrently possess the following characteristics:
(1) forming a relatively stable criminal organization with a large number of members, having clear organizers and leaders, with core members being basically fixed;
(2) obtaining economic benefits through organized illegal or criminal activities or other means, having a certain economic strength to support the activities of the organization;
(3) repeatedly engaging in organized illegal or criminal activities by means of violence, threats, or other means, committing evil deeds, bullying and harming the masses;
(4) through committing illegal or criminal activities, or by taking advantage of the protection or connivance of state functionaries, dominating one area, forming illegal control or major influence within a certain region or industry, seriously disrupting the economic and social order.
Now this interpretation is hereby announced.
